# The optional modules this release can install (docs/modules.md).
#
# While this file holds nothing but comments, the release carries no module
# catalogue: scripts/build-release-bundle.sh builds none, install.sh carries no
# digest for it and refuses --module, and the core reports "no catalogue".
#
# A module is four lines. <NAME> is upper case letters, digits and underscores
# and starts with a letter; the name of the module on a box is <NAME> in lower
# case with each underscore a hyphen (VIRT is virt, VIRT_MANAGEMENT is
# virt-management). One assignment to a line, no spaces, no quotes, no comment
# after a value.
#
#   MODULE_<NAME>_TAG        the tag of the module's release: v<number>.<number>.<number>
#   MODULE_<NAME>_COMMIT     the commit that tag must name: 40 lower case hexadecimal digits
#   MODULE_<NAME>_COMPONENT  the module's repository in the ReCasaOS organisation
#   MODULE_<NAME>_TIER       core (maintained here, proven on a real machine) or community
#
# The release build reads checksums.txt and the two archives (amd64 and arm64)
# of that release, checks the tag against the commit, and fails if anything does
# not hold: there is no catalogue with some of its modules missing.
MODULE_VIRT_TAG=v0.1.2
MODULE_VIRT_COMMIT=b363954982ff337f3ad273b42fbfa6d997957120
MODULE_VIRT_COMPONENT=CasaOS-VirtManagement
MODULE_VIRT_TIER=community
